gcc 4.4.7 (RHEL/CentOS 6 system compiler) compatibility for the vendored
pocketsphinx 5.0.4 in sphinx-asr 7745786. Applied by
baselines/rhel6/guest/provision-guest.sh with `patch -p1` in the guest copy
only; the sphinx-asr submodule is never modified.

Declaration-only changes; no generated code changes:

1. Repeated typedefs. C11 (and gcc >= 4.6) accept a typedef repeated with
   the same type; gcc 4.4 rejects it in every mode ("error: redefinition of
   typedef"). ps_config_t and ps_decoder_t are typedef'd in
   pocketsphinx/model.h and pocketsphinx/search.h, which pocketsphinx.h
   includes, and again in pocketsphinx.h. fsg_model_t is typedef'd in
   pocketsphinx/model.h and again by src/lm/fsg_model.h. Drop the repeats.

2. Storage-class order. With PS_USE_THREAD_LOCAL_RNG, PS_THREAD_LOCAL is
   gcc's __thread on gcc 4.4 (no C11 _Thread_local). gcc requires __thread
   to follow `static` ("error: '__thread' before 'static'"), while C11
   _Thread_local may come first. Write `static PS_THREAD_LOCAL`, valid for
   both.

diff -u a/vendor/pocketsphinx/include/pocketsphinx.h b/vendor/pocketsphinx/include/pocketsphinx.h
--- a/vendor/pocketsphinx/include/pocketsphinx.h
+++ b/vendor/pocketsphinx/include/pocketsphinx.h
@@ -126,14 +126,14 @@ typedef struct ps_arg_s {
 /**
  * @struct ps_config_t
  * @brief configuration object.
+ * (typedef lives in pocketsphinx/model.h; C99 forbids repeating it)
  */
-typedef struct cmd_ln_s ps_config_t;
 
 /**
  * @struct ps_decoder_t
  * @brief Speech recognizer object.
+ * (typedef lives in pocketsphinx/search.h; C99 forbids repeating it)
  */
-typedef struct ps_decoder_s ps_decoder_t;
 
 /**
  * @struct ps_nbest_t
